    "https://jobs.belmont.edu/ux/ats/careersite/10/home/requisition/4944?c=belmont": {
      "title": "Current Openings",
      "description": "Current Openings - belmont Skip to Main Content Sign In Create Profile English (US) Job Category Search NOTE: If you are a current Belmont employee, please login to myBelmont and apply through the Internal Jobs Career Center in Belmont Be You . (This does not apply to students.) Filters Reset Country United States (259) Date Posted Within 1 day (2) Within 3 days (6) Within 7 days (11) Within 15 days (19) Within 30 days (46) Anytime (259) Job Category Exempt (Staff) (13) Non-Exempt (Staff) (23) Lecturer (1) Adjunct (79) Tenure Track (Faculty) (24) Non-Tenure Track (Faculty) (6) Student Employment (64) Federal Work Study Student Emp (48) Graduate Assistant (1) Current Openings Create an alert Assistant Professor of Mathematics United States 9/15/2026 Assistant Professor Computer Science United States 9/15/2026 Pharmacy Operations Fellow in Drug Information United States 9/15/2026 Clinical Management Fellow in Drug Information United States 9/15/2026 Venue Operations Crew United States 9/14/2026 Event Coordinator United States 9/14/2026 Budget Assistant United States 9/11/2026 Learning Spaces and Outreach Coordinator United States 9/11/2026 HUB - Graduate Assistant United States 9/11/2026 College of Sciences & Mathematics - Undergraduate Research Laboratory Monitor United States 9/11/2026 Assistant/Associate Professor of Sport Administration United States 9/10/2026 Enrollment, Office of VP - Admissions Assistant United States 9/8/2026 HUB - Student Assistant United States 9/8/2026 FCOM, Dean's Office - Student Assistant United States 9/8/2026 Department Chair, Public Health United States 9/8/2026 Marketing and Communications - Video Assistant United States 9/8/2026 Social Sciences - Office Assistant United States 9/8/2026 Admissions Coordinator (Temporary) United States 9/1/2026 Assistant Professor of Political Science United States 9/1/2026 PR/Content Specialist United States 8/28/2026 Web Specialist United States 8/28/2026 Temporary Part-Time Program Assistant - CMPA United States 8/28/2026 Academic Advising Administrative Assistant United States 8/27/2026 Engagement Officer for Reunions and Honors United States 8/27/2026 Student Success & Flourishing Coordinator United States 8/27/2026 1 2 3 4 ... 11 Create an alert And get notified by email as soon as a job matches with your criteria. Name Label * Cadence Daily Weekly Your criteria Create Cancel Cannot create an alert You must update your profile and provide an e-mail address before setting up an alert. Close Create an alert You'll need to apply at least one search or filter before creating a job alert. Close Belmont University is a Christ-centered community. The University faculty, administration, and staff uphold Jesus as the Christ and as the measure for all things. As a community seeking to uphold Christian standards of morality, ethics, and conduct, Belmont University holds high expectations of each person who chooses to join the community. In compliance with federal law, including provisions of Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973/the Americans with Disabilities Act, Belmont University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, national or ethnic origin, age, disability, military service, or sexual orientation in its administration of education policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or employment. Consistent with applicable civil rights law, the University primarily hires employees of the Christian faith who are committed to support the mission of the University. The University has appointed the Chief Human Resources Officer/Deputy Title IX Coordinator to serve as coordinator of non-discrimination compliance for staff and faculty. The Director of Institutional Equity and Compliance and Title IX Coordinator serves as coordinator of compliance for Title IX (sex discrimination) issues and questions for students. Click here to learn more. *In accordance with accrediting standards for its professional education programs in law and medicine, the University does not apply religious criteria in hiring employees within those programs. All employees hired by the University, regardless of religious faith, shall be committed to Belmont’s Christ-centered, student-focused mission. Belmont's Office of Human Resources will conduct ongoing evaluations of the means by which candidates for employment are sought, to the end that the pool of candidates will include qualified women, minorities, veterans and disabled individuals. Belmont University is an equal opportunity employer under all applicable civil rights laws."
    },
